<!-- @after 14. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- **No hard-coded strings:** placeholders instead of concatenation, and `<plurals>` with `%d` even in the `one` form.
- **Format numbers, dates and currency with the locale's formatters;** keep money out of `Double`.
- **Lay out with start and end,** mirror directional icons, and test right-to-left with the AR (XB) pseudolocale.
- **Per-app language:** AppCompat 1.6+ backports it to Android 12 and lower; on Android 13+, generate the locale config so the language appears in system settings.
- **Server text follows `Accept-Language`** with a fallback chain, for example es-MX → es → en.
